You are debugging a production issue where an order-processing Spring Boot service fails to persist records reliably and occasionally encounters database connection leaks. A developer submitted the following refactored method intended to perform asynchronous order processing:

java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    @Autowired
    private OrderRepository orderRepository;

    @Transactional
    public CompletableFuture<Order> processOrder(OrderRequest request) {
        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {
            Order order = new Order(request);
            return orderRepository.save(order);
        });
    }
}

You are debugging a production issue where an aggregation service hangs indefinitely under sustained concurrent load. The service uses a dedicated thread pool to process parent requests and their subtasks as shown in the following snippet:

java
@Service
public class AggregationService {
    private final ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(8);

    public CompletableFuture<Report> generateReport(List<String> userIds) {
        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> {
            List<CompletableFuture<UserData>> futures = userIds.stream()
                .map(id -> CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> fetchUserData(id), pool))
                .toList();

            CompletableFuture.allOf(futures.toArray(new CompletableFuture[0])).join();
            return buildReport(futures);
        }, pool);
    }
}
